  "query_preview": "..\nNext 7 days (through Friday)...\n\nConditions remain hot and mostly dry today, although less so than\nyesterday, ahead of an approaching trough. As a result, fire\nweather concerns remain elevated. As surface wind turn out of the\neast late today, increasing atmospheric moisture, there is a low \nchance (5-20%) for showers and thunderstorms near the Dakota \nborder late today into early Sunday.\n\nThe next best chance for precipitation (40-90%) then arrives late\nSunday into Monday as the upper level trough moves across the \nregion and PWATs increase to 170-210% of normal. With this, any \nshower or thunderstorm will be capable of producing pockets of \nheavy rain, especially over the west and the north. A few storms \nmay be strong to severe Sunday afternoon and evening over the\nnorth and east, with strong wind gusts as the main threat. The \narrival of this trough will also allow temperatures to cool, with \nhighs in the 70s over the west to 80s over the east by Monday.\n\nTuesday into the end of the work week, models now favor a modest \nridge building in. This will keep conditions mostly dry and allow\ntemperatures near (70s) to slightly above (80s) normal to continue.\nArcher",
